        "t": "text",
        "v": "Both retrieval and tools fix the knowledge property, but they fix different halves of it. Retrieval supplies documents: policies, manuals, past tickets, anything that is text and changes on a schedule. A live-state tool supplies the current value of something: an order status, an inventory count, a balance. The course names one common design error explicitly: retrieval doing a job that live-state should own. [1]"
